From 97e983fdd2f600a2d4bbb81e18535ee6b3ac38ee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Z User <z@container>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 22:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] classes: conversions + identity + the builtin singletons
 (citadel r3, patch 33)

- === : word identity (C11), total, never dispatchable. 1 === 1.0 is true -
  both are the double 1.0, there is no public int box; the visible edge is
  0.0 === -0.0 (false) while 0.0 == -0.0 stays true
- is (C12): classof + identity fused, the exact-class probe; isinstance/
  classof as plain native builtins for the chain walk and the class value
- operator <Target> rides the as lane (C13): user conversions dispatch like
  operator methods (receiver staged, result type-checked - a subclass of the
  target is legal), inherited down the chain, private ones hierarchy-internal
- the seven builtin class singletons (C10): str/num/bool/array/map/function/
  nil under Object, frozen at birth, bound as top-level values through ONE
  seed table (the old two hand-built arrays were position-paired by
  discipline); classof(null) === nil, classof(Class) === Class
- TAG_AS + TT_ + the hidden ' str' globals die; tag id 6 stays reserved
- three bugs fixed: the guard-stack overflow in vm_init_singletons
  (OK_GC_GUARD_CAPACITY 16, silently exceeded - the str singleton's name was
  swept mid-startup and reused by the num name; discipline is per-object
  balanced and checked now), the asprint leak in the as_str object arms
  (lsan, first exposed by instance-as-str), and as_num's missing int return
  + copy-paste message + missing instance/class/method arms
- operators_subscript.ok split: its error-lane directive made the whole file
  skip output comparison, hiding a wrong expect (40 vs the correct 45)

